WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Have you ever wondered
if there’s a natural way

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.160
to lower your high blood pressure,
guard against Alzheimer's,

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.440
lose weight, and feel better?
Well, it turns out there is!

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.680
Welcome to the
NutritionFacts Podcast.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.240
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:22.160
There’s a common type of heart condition
that causes irregular heartbeats.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.400
It’s called atrial fibrillation,
or AFib for short,

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.560
and more and more people
every year are diagnosed with it.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:36.560
Today we start with the best foods to eat
and avoid to decrease our risk of AFib.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:40.960
Atrial fibrillation, or Afib, is the
most common clinical arrhythmia,

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:43.120
meaning abnormal heart rhythm,

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:47.440
affecting millions of Americans,
recognized as a global public

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.080
health problem due to its
significant burden of death and

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:55.400
disease resulting from stroke,
heart attacks, and heart failure.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:59.680
Is there any particular diet that
may help prevent or treat it?

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:02.800
Well, recently we learned
what not to eat.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:06.920
Low-carb diets are associated
with increased risk of developing

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:10.200
atrial fibrillation for
a variety of reasons.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.880
First of all, people on low-carb diets
may be eating fewer anti-inflammatory

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.160
foods like vegetables,
fruits, and whole grains.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:21.640
Reducing intake of these
anti-inflammatory foods may be

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:26.560
one of the important mechanisms
for the risk of getting Afib.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.520
Secondly, a low-carbohydrate diet

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.200
means increased protein
and fat consumption,

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:35.920
which may stimulate oxidative stress,
the formation of free radicals,

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:39.760
which was also demonstrated
to be associated with Afib.

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:42.720
Finally, the effect could result
from the increased risk

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:47.200
of other cardiovascular disease,
which can set you up for Afib,

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.000
and indeed, low-carb diets are
associated with an increased risk

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.560
of overall mortality, dying
from any cause, as well as

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:58.280
specifically dying from cardiovascular
disease and dying from cancer.

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:02.040
Dietary recommendations for patients
with heart rhythm disorders

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:05.880
is essentially the opposite of
a low-carb diet, centered on

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:10.000
a day-to-day basis around fruits,
vegetables, grains, beans,

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.280
and nuts, with seafood at
most a few days a week;

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:17.320
eggs, dairy, and chicken on
more like a once-a-week basis;

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:20.880
and other meat on more like
a once-a-month basis, in part

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:25.120
because we're trying to cut down
on saturated and trans fats.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:28.200
Whole-food plant-based diets
emphasizing whole grains,

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:31.080
legumes (beans, split peas,
chickpeas, and lentils),

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.400
vegetables, fruits and nuts

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:36.480
and excluding most (or all) animal
products may play a special role,

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:38.960
as they not only maximize
protective foods,

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:42.240
but also exclude potentially
harmful animal foods.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:44.520
For example, there is persuasive
evidence that avoidance

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:48.200
of certain foods may beneficially
affect atrial fibrillation,

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:51.240
such as the avoidance
of dark fish and alcohol.

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:54.960
The dark fish thing comes from
the Framingham Heart Study.

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:58.280
By dark fish, they mean
salmon, swordfish, bluefish,

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.240
mackerel, and sardines.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.320
And they found in an exploratory
analysis that those participants

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.720
who consumed more than
4 servings of darkfish

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:08.600
like salmon or sardines a week
were at a whopping

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:12.400
6-fold higher risk of
developing Afib, though

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:16.360
the intake of fish in general
didn't seem to have any effect.

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:19.400
We're not exactly sure why
alcohol is so bad when

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.000
it comes to arrhythmias,

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.880
but we might have as
much as an 8% increase

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:25.440
in the relative risk of Afib

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:29.120
associated with each drink
one might have per day,

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:32.200
though drinking coffee or caffeine
in general does not seem

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:36.080
to be related to arrhythmia risk.

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:38.560
Where plant-based diets
really shine, though,

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:41.320
is in Afib risk factor management.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.400
Plant-based diets may
reduce the likelihood of many

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:47.000
traditional risk factors that are
associated with Afib, including

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:51.880
hypertension, hyperthyroidism,
obesity, and diabetes.

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:54.240
High blood pressure is one
of the major risk factors,

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:57.800
accounting for about one-fifth
of all new cases of Afib,

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:00.320
which is where plant-based
diets can come in:

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:04.360
improving vasodilation, the ability
for your arteries to expand naturally,

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:07.400
in addition to the anti-inflammatory
and antioxidant effects, and

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:08.960
increased potassium intake,

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:12.920
and decreased blood
viscosity or sludginess.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:16.760
In terms of hyperthyroidism,
excluding all animal foods

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:20.240
from one's diet was associated
with half the prevalence

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:23.600
of hyperthyroidism compared
with those who eat meat,

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:27.080
with vegetarians and
fish-only diets associated

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:29.440
with intermediate protection.

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:32.400
Having excess body fat may
be responsible for about

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:37.680
another fifth of all Afib cases.
But the good news is significantÂ&nbsp;

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:38.760
weight loss is associated

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:42.520
with a 6-fold greater freedom
from atrial fibrillation.

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:45.840
You can see that those with Afib
who started out overweight, but

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.040
lost 10% or more of
their body weight,

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:51.400
5 years later only 10%
ended up with Afib,

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:54.160
whereas those who lost less
than 3% or gained weight,

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:58.440
60% ended up with Afib,
6 times more.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:01.920
Here are all the atrial fibrillation
risk factors that can be prevented,

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:05.720
arrested or even reversed with a
healthy enough plant-based diet:

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:09.160
high blood pressure, type 2
diabetes, obesity, systemic

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:13.080
inflammation, and heart disease.
In light of these findings,

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:17.240
dietary modifications are
of paramount importance.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:21.280
But you don't know if it could
actually cure atrial fibrillation

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:25.200
until you put it to the test.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.520
Unfortunately, all we
have are case reports,

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:29.320
but this one is quite compelling.

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:33.040
An 82-year-old man
presents with polypharmacy,

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:35.920
meaning on a bunch of
different medications due to

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:38.680
coronary artery disease,
a heart attack history,

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:41.520
ischemic cardiomyopathy,
high cholesterol,

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:45.120
high blood pressure, and
persistent atrial fibrillation, who

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:51.200
presented with memory loss, cognitive
impairment, fatigue and weakness.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:54.960
Now, if you're not going to change
the diet and lifestyle that led to all

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:57.720
the problems in the first place,
then drugs can certainly be

00:05:57.720 --> 00:05:59.240
better than nothing.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:01.840
Yet commonly used blood pressure
and cholesterol-lowering

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:05.560
medications provide actually
little absolute risk reduction

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:10.680
and pose significant risk of adverse
effects, as I've explored before.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:15.400
So this guy decided to start
treating the underlying cause.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:18.800
So he started a whole-food
plant-based diet with moderate

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:21.920
physical activity, resulting in a rapid
reduction of high cholesterol

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:24.400
and high blood pressure,
and the discontinuation

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:28.600
of statin, antihypertensive,
and beta blocker drug therapy.

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:31.760
The patient also reported
reversal of impaired cognition

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:33.960
and symptoms associated
with atrial fibrillation

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.440
and ischemic cardiomyopathy,

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:39.320
including light-headedness,
fatigue, and weakness.

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:43.920
Check out these numbers.
Started out on all his medications.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.040
Started eating healthier in February

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:50.480
and his LDL bad cholesterol
dropped 37% down to 72.

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:54.400
And you say, yeah, but he's still on
cholesterol-lowering statin drugs.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:59.320
But even after his doctor discontinued
it, and his blood pressure meds,

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:00.800
his cholesterol stayed down,

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:05.080
and his blood pressure
completely normalized.

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:07.840
OK, but what happened
to his atrial fibrillation?

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:10.720
Completely resolved.

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:13.920
Here's how the patient described it.

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:17.320
"In December 2017, I suffered
a near-fatal heart attack

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:20.840
and was rushed to the hospital.
I immediately had a stent put in.

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:21.440
The following day,

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:25.000
I was prescribed a number of
drugs to manage my condition.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:28.960
My brain fog got worse
and I felt tired all the time.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:31.240
I decided enough was enough.

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:35.080
I had already lost four years of my life
to medication-induced brain fog;

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:37.600
I wasn't going to sacrifice more.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:40.600
I had been eating a wholesome
Mediterranean diet,

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:44.400
but I was then educated on the
benefits of cutting out all the crap.

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:47.400
And now? I have the strength
to lift weights and walk

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.360
and run on the treadmill
an hour every day.

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:51.960
I feel more alive
than I have for years.

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:54.800
I wake up each morning with
a clear head and happy heart,

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:58.600
grateful to not have to
take a handful of drugs.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:01.840
Even though I'm not perfect
with my diet, I've seen huge

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:03.320
benefits from eating this way.

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:05.680
My blood tests have shown
remarkable improvement,

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:08.760
which keeps me motivated
to stay on track.

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:11.440
Because of my improvement,
my cardiologist suggested

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:15.000
I could let go of his
last remaining drug.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:20.520
Eating this food gave me an
opportunity to reclaim my health.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:21.320
In our next story,

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:24.040
we look at how fish
and fish oil consumption

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:26.720
do not appear to protect
against heart disease,

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:28.260
arrhythmias,
or sudden death.

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:31.000
So why would they
increase cancer risk?

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:34.640
2013 was a bad year for fish oil.

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:37.720
Claims were crushed that
the long chain omega 3's

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:41.600
in fish oil, EPA, and DHA would stop
the progression of heart disease.

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:45.280
And then DHA was associated with
increased risk of prostate cancer,

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:50.200
and monumentally failed
to treat macular degeneration.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:54.120
This over-the-top rhetoric
sounded a little suspicious

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:58.600
and indeed the paper was retracted
because the author sells some

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:04.000
rival supplement that he failed to
disclose, but he does have a point.

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:07.120
I covered the fish oil
failure for heart disease.

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:09.760
What about the
increased cancer risk?

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:12.480
Men with the highest
circulating levels in their blood

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:14.960
of the long chain
omega 3 fat DHA

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:18.240
were found to be at higher
risk for prostate cancer,

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:21.880
though a subsequent compilation
of all such studies suggested EPA,

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:25.120
the other major long chain
omega 3 in fish and fish oil

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:28.360
may be more closely associated
with increased cancer risk.

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:31.600
Either way, these long chain
omega 3's have been promoted

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:34.680
for prevention of heart
disease and cancer,

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:37.840
but now that we know that not
only does there appear to be

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:40.440
no benefit for death,
heart attack, or stroke,

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:44.040
but that there may be an
elevation in cancer risk,

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:46.720
the general recommendation to
increase the intake of these fats

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:50.160
should consider
its potential risks.

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:54.280
How could eating more fish
or fish oil increase cancer risk?

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:57.960
Well, there are some industrial
pollutants like PCBs linked

00:09:57.960 --> 00:10:03.840
to increased prostate cancer risk,
and the primary source of exposure

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:06.040
in the general population is
believed to be through diet

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:08.120
from fish, meat, and
dairy products.

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:11.920
If you do a supermarket survey,
the PCBs, shown in white here,

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:19.440
are highest in freshwater fish, and
lowest in vegans — cannibals take note.

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:23.560
No, that's just how they label the
market basket of plant foods,

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:27.840
though vegans have been tested and
were found to be significantly

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:32.449
less polluted, including the PCB
specifically linked to prostate cancer.

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:36.400
And so maybe the confounding factor
was meat consumption in general,

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:40.160
not just fish, and that lower meat
consumption may be a reason

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:44.240
for the lower rates of prostate
cancer in the lower DHA group,

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:47.200
as the consumption of well-done meat
is associated with an increased risk

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:50.960
of prostate cancer and
intake should be restricted.

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:54.680
We also used to think omega 3's
could protect us from arrhythmias —

00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:58.360
abnormal heart rhythms
like atrial fibrillation.

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:03.320
Millions suffer from the condition,
which causes an irregular heartbeat

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:06.320
and a higher risk
of stroke and death,

00:11:06.320 --> 00:11:09.640
but fish and fish oil consumption
does not appear effective

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:12.960
for preventing it
or treating it.

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:17.040
Other arrhythmias can be life
threatening and cause sudden death.

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:20.760
Despite initial encouraging
results, more recent studies

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:24.200
have not only failed to reduce sudden
cardiac death with omega 3's,

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:27.280
but actually increased
mortality in cardiac patients.

00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:30.960
For example, men with heart disease
advised to eat more oily fish

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:34.760
or supplied with fish oil capsules
were found to have a higher risk

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:40.480
of cardiac death, maybe because of the
contaminants in fish such as mercury?

00:11:40.480 --> 00:11:45.840
In either case, given the inconsistent
benefits and the potential adverse

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:48.240
effects, omega 3's
must be prescribed

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:50.840
with caution and generalized
recommendations to increase

00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:56.880
fish intake or to take fish oil capsules
need to be reconsidered.

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:57.640
Finally today,

00:11:57.640 --> 00:12:01.080
did you know that a cup a day
of beans, chickpeas, or lentils

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:03.520
for three months may
slow resting heart rate

00:12:03.520 --> 00:12:08.600
as much as exercising for
50 hours on a treadmill?

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:10.760
The accumulated weight
of evidence linking

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:14.040
elevated resting heart rate
to a shortened lifespan—

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:16.280
even in apparently
healthy individuals,

00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:18.160
makes a strong case for
it to be considered

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:20.080
in the assessment
of risk.

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:21.960
It’s got strong advantages.

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:24.000
Taking one’s pulse
is cheap,

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:25.080
takes little time,

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:26.960
it’s understandable
to people,

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:28.800
and it’s something
everyone can do at home

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:32.280
to measure their progress to
become an active participant

00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:34.760
in their own
health management.

00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:37.400
Every ten beats
per minute increase

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:39.720
is associated with
a 10 to 20% increase

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:42.240
in the risk of death.

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:44.800
There seems to be a
continuous increase in risk

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:46.840
with increasing
heart rate,

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:49.840
at least for values above
about a beat a second.

00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:51.600
So we can just look
at our watch

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:55.040
and if our heart is beating faster
than the seconds go by—

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:57.800
even when we’re
sitting quietly,

00:12:57.800 --> 00:12:59.720
then we have to do
something about it,

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:02.880
especially when we start
getting up around 80 or 90.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:05.240
Men with no apparent
heart disease evidence

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:07.680
with a pulse of 90 may
have five times higher risk

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:09.160
of sudden cardiac death—

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:12.000
meaning their first symptom
is their last—

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.280
compared to those down
the safety zone.

00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:17.160
Living up around 90 increases
heart disease risk

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:19.440
at a level similar
to smoking.

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:23.400
If you ask most doctors, though,
90 is considered normal.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:25.760
The accepted limits of heartrate
have long been set

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:27.360
at 60 and 100 beats/min.

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:30.720
How did they come
up with that?

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:34.400
It was adopted as a
matter of convenience

00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:39.360
just based on the scale of
the squares on EKG paper.

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:42.600
A historical accident like
the QWERTY keyboard

00:13:42.600 --> 00:13:45.080
that just became the norm.

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:48.960
60 to 100 doesn’t even
represent the bell curve.

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:51.640
These cardiologists measured
the heart rate of 500 people

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:55.000
and concluded that
45 to 95 was a better

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:56.680
definition of normal,

00:13:56.680 --> 00:13:59.120
rounding to 50 to 90,

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:02.600
which a survey of leading
cardiologists concurred with.

00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:06.120
Now we know that normal
doesn’t necessarily mean optimal,

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:08.280
but doctors shouldn’t be
telling people with heart rates

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:09.720
in the 50’s that they're
are too low;

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:13.680
in fact they may be right
where they should be.

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:15.920
Certainly a heart rate
higher than 80

00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:17.800
should ring an alarm bell,

00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:20.360
but what can we
do about it?

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:23.640
Exercise is one
obvious possibility.

00:14:23.640 --> 00:14:25.960
Ironically, you make
the heart go faster

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:27.160
so that that the
rest of the time

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:29.040
your heart beats slower.

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:32.800
The public health benefits
of physical exercise,

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:35.320
especially for heart protection,
are widely accepted,

00:14:35.320 --> 00:14:38.920
and among the many biological
mechanisms proposed

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:41.360
to account for this
risk-reducing effect

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:44.000
is autonomic nervous system
regulation of the heart.

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:46.680
That’s your brain’s
ability to slow down

00:14:46.680 --> 00:14:48.280
the resting beat
of our heart.

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:51.360
If you put people through
a 12 week aerobic

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:53.440
conditioning program
of cycling, stairmaster,

00:14:53.440 --> 00:14:55.000
and running on
a treadmill,

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:57.080
you can drop their
resting heart rate down

00:14:57.080 --> 00:15:00.120
from about 69
to about 66,

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:04.080
so three beats
per minute drop.

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:05.800
Of course you have
to keep it up;

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:07.680
stop exercising and your
resting heart rate

00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:09.880
goes right back up.

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:12.280
Exercise is just one way
to drop our heartrate, though.

00:15:12.280 --> 00:15:16.320
The way to our heart may also
be through our stomach.

00:15:16.320 --> 00:15:18.120
What if instead of
three months of exercise,

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:20.240
you did three months
of beans?

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:23.800
A cup a day of beans,
chickpeas, or lentils.

00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:26.280
The first randomized
controlled trial of beans

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:27.880
for the treatment
of diabetes.

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:31.200
And indeed successfully
improved blood sugar control

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:32.480
dropping A1C levels

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:34.040
from 7.4 to 6.9,

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:36.160
but this was also
the first study

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:38.280
to ever assess the effect
of bean consumption

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:39.720
on heart rate.

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:42.560
And indeed one of the few
to determine the effect

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:45.840
on heartrate of any
dietary intervention.

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:48.280
This is particularly important
in diabetics

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:50.480
since having a higher
resting heart rate

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:52.320
not only increases the
risk of death

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:53.680
just like everybody else,

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:55.960
but also appears to
predict greater risk

00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:57.720
of diabetic complications,

00:15:57.720 --> 00:16:00.440
such as damage to the
nerves and eyes.

00:16:00.440 --> 00:16:03.400
So how did beans do?

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:06.520
A 3.4 beat drop
in heartrate—

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:10.160
just as much as the 250 hours
on a treadmill.

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:13.040
We’re not sure why beans
are as powerful as exercise

00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:16.560
in bringing down one’s
resting heart rate.

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:19.520
In addition to the potential
direct beneficial effects

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:21.040
of all the good stuff
in legumes,

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:23.800
there is also the potential
displacement value

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:26.200
of reducing some of
the animal protein foods

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:28.440
by eating so
many beans instead.

00:16:28.440 --> 00:16:35.040
Regardless, we should consider
eating pulses for our pulse.

